.TH ROLLING_FLASH 8 "2026-11-20" "rolling-linux 2.1.11" "Rolling WWAN Services Manual"
.SH NAME
rolling_flash \- firmware download and upgrade service for Rolling Wireless WWAN devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/bin/rolling_flash
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rolling_flash
is the firmware update, switch and recovery service of the Rolling
Linux apps set.  It is started by
.BR systemd (1)
as
.B rolling_flash.service
and runs as a system daemon; it is not normally started by hand.
.PP
On start-up the service reads the OEM\-specific update configuration
.B FwUpdate.ini
(seeded into
.IR /etc/rolling/config_file/rolling_flash_service/ ,
see
.BR FwUpdate.ini (5))
and drives the modem firmware update flow from there.  Firmware
payloads are consumed from the directory
.IR /var/lib/rolling/rolling_fw_pkg ,
which must be populated by the OEM\-provided
.I fw_package
before the service is used.
.PP
Firmware switching uses the
.B fastboot
protocol; install the
.B fastboot
tool on the target system if firmware switch operations are required
(apt\-get install fastboot).
.PP
A configuration reload can be requested by sending the service a SIGHUP
(systemctl reload rolling_flash.service).
.SH OPTIONS
.B rolling_flash
takes no command\-line options; it is managed through systemd and the
configuration file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/rolling/config_file/rolling_flash_service/FwUpdate.ini
Runtime update configuration.  Seeded from the shipped templates at
install time or first boot, and never overwritten afterwards, so local
edits survive upgrades.
.TP
.I /usr/share/linux\-apps/flash_set/<project>_<oem>/
Per\-OEM configuration templates shipped by the package.
.TP
.I /var/lib/rolling/rolling_fw_pkg
Firmware package payloads (created by the package post\-install
script; populated from the OEM fw_package).
.SH SYSTEMD
.B rolling_flash.service
is ordered after
.B ModemManager.service
and
.BR rolling_helper.service .
ExecReload re\-reads the configuration on SIGHUP.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
systemctl daemon\-reload
systemctl enable rolling_flash.service
systemctl start rolling_flash.service
systemctl status rolling_flash.service
.fi
.PP
Watch the service journal:
.nf
journalctl \-u rolling_flash.service
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rolling_config (8),
.BR rolling_helper (8),
.BR rolling_ma (8),
.BR FwUpdate.ini (5),
.BR fastboot (1),
.BR systemd (1)
